  "contentHtml": "\n\n                    <!-- Display video article in news article for the custom next story -->\n                    \n                    <!-- Modifying the body placing embeds,promoslots,related etc.-->\n                                        <figure><img src=\"/images/default.jpg\" alt=\"\"></figure><p>New Delhi: <a href=\"/tag/park+medi+world\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Park Medi World</a> Ltd on Tuesday announced the incorporation of a wholly-owned subsidiary, <a href=\"/tag/park+medicity+prayagraj+ltd\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Park Medicity Prayagraj Ltd</a>, to develop and operate a 550-bed multi-super-speciality hospital in Uttar Pradesh.The new entity has been established to execute a project awarded to the company under the Public-Private Partnership (PPP) model by the <a href=\"/tag/prayagraj\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Prayagraj</a> Municipal Corporation, the company said in a regulatory filing.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>The subsidiary was incorporated on Tuesday, with Park Medi World subscribing to 1,50,000 equity shares at a face value of Rs 10 each, amounting to a total cost of Rs 15 lakh, it said.</p>\n                            <p>Advt\n                            </p>\n\n                              \n                                                         \n                        <p>Park Medi World owns 100 per cent shareholding in the newly formed healthcare services entity, the filing added.Founded in 2000, Park Medi World claims to be the second-largest <a href=\"/tag/private+hospital+chain+in+north+india\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">private hospital chain in North India</a> and the largest private hospital chain in terms of bed capacity in Haryana. The company operates a network of 16 multi-super speciality hospitals under the 'Park' brand across Haryana, Punjab, Rajasthan, Delhi and Uttar Pradesh. PTI                    </p><!-- Category Most Read Placement -->\n                                                                    \n                                                                \n                                <ul>\n                                    \n\n                                                                        <li><a href=\"/agency/87654375/PTI\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">PTI</a></li>\n                                </ul>\n                                <ul>\n                                    <!-- <li> Updated On Sep 9, 2026 at 07:28 AM IST</li> -->\n                                    <li>Published On Sep 9, 2026 at 07:28 AM IST</li>\n                                    <!-- <li class=\"desktop-view\">1 min read</li> -->\n                                </ul>\n                            \n                                        \n\n                    \n\n                    <!-- Comment Section -->\n                                            \n                                        <!-- Comment Section -->\n\n                    \n                      \n    \n            <p>\n                </p><h2>Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. </h2>   \n                <h3>Subscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights &amp; analysis in your inbox.</h3>\n            <p></p>\n\n            <!-- <figure class=\"top-newsletter-subs__icon-nl\" role=\"presentation\" aria-label=\"Newsletter icon\">\n                <img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://st.etb2bimg.com/Themes/Release/theme4/images/icons/icon-newsletter.svg\" alt=\"Newsletter icon\" width=\"55\" height=\"55\">\n            </figure> -->\n        \n            \n                \n                    <h2>All about ETHealthworld industry right on your smartphone! </h2>\n                    <ul>\n                        <li><a href=\"/app\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Download the ETHealthworld App</a> and get the Realtime updates and Save your favourite articles